Question title:Simplify the Compilation Process
Question link:https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/9kh4giios2j4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg
solution:
touch build.sh
echo "gcc hello.c -o hello" >build.sh
chmod +x build.sh
./build.sh
./hello

Approach:
1.first created the empty file build.sh
2.entered the shebang for the c that is gcc hello.c -o hello and initialised to the build.sh
3.gave the permission to execute
4.print commands ./build.sh and ./hello
